  "processObserver": {
    "method": "docker top every 100 ms; a process that reads as unrestricted is re-read once after a short delay and counted as a violation only when the same pid still runs the same program and still carries no restriction",
    "invariantUnchanged": "The node builds --postprocessor-args ffmpeg:-threads 1 on its only yt-dlp spawn path unconditionally, so a real unrestricted process is still unrestricted on the re-read and still fails the lane. Only a read the observer could not complete is excluded, and an unmeasured process is not evidence of a violation.",
    "unconfirmedReadsAreNotPasses": "Reads that could not be confirmed are reported as ytDlpUnconfirmedFfmpegThreadRestrictionTotal and ffmpegUnconfirmedRestrictionReadTotal rather than folded into the restriction booleans.",
    "observedExecWindowReads": "One observation of 471 sampled eight yt-dlp processes and read one of them mid-execve, before its argv was written. The re-read showed the restriction, so it was recorded as unconfirmed and no violation was counted.",
    "confirmingRun": "A second capacity run at this anchor on the same host produced ffmpegThreadRestrictionProven true with zero unconfirmed reads. The two runs agree on the boolean; this record is the later of the two."
